cts across the full separator line and color the gap with the separator color.\n 124: \n 125:     Input structure:\n 126:     - A dominant background contains one full-width or full-height one-pixel\n 127:       separator line in a non-background color.\n 128:     - One other foreground color forms solid rectangular objects, all strictly on the same side of that separator.\n 129:     - Remaining non-background pixels are scattered distractors.\n 130: \n 131:     Rule:\n 132:     - Keep the input grid shape and unchanged pixels outside each affected corridor.\n 133:     - Mirror each source object across the separator line.\n 134:     - For every source object, recolor the rectangular strip between the\n 135:       original object and its reflection to the separator color, then paint the\n 136:       reflected object in the source color.\n 137: \n 138:     Key insight:\n 139:     - The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified\n 140:       structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while\n 141:       scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.\n 142:     \"\"\"\n 143:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n 144:     bg = get_bg(g)\n 145:     orient, axis, axis_color = _find_separator(g, bg)\n 146:     source_color, components = _find_source(g, bg, orient, axis, axis_color)\n 147: \n 148:     out = g.copy()\n 149:     for component in components:\n 150:         _mirror_and_connect(out, component, orient, axis, axis_color, source_color)\n 151:     return out\n 152: \n 153: # --------------- generator (att2, o5x) ---------------\n 154: \n 155: # Canvas and palette.\n 156: GRID_SIZE_RANGE = (18, 23)\n 157: COLOR_COUNT = 10\n 158: PALETTE_SIZE = 4\n 159: ORIENTATIONS = (\"vertical\", \"horizontal\")\n 160: AXIS_RATIO_RANGE = (0.35, 0.50)\n 161: SIDES = (-1, 1)\n 162: \n 163: # Source rectangles and reflected corridors.\n 164: SOURCE_RECT_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 3)\n 165: RECT_HEIGHT_RANGE = (2, 5)\n 166: 